#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0083 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "BOUNDARY -- pins finding SD0083-F1. USUBJID S1-001 appears twice but under DIFFERENT STUDYIDs (S1 and S2), so the key tuple (USUBJID, STUDYID) is distinct and nothing fires. This is the boundary between the sheet row 90 DESCRIPTION's two sentences: sentence 1 ('USUBJID must be unique for each subject ACROSS ALL TRIALS in the submission') is NOT what the Check tests, sentence 2 ('in the DM domain there should only be one record per subject') is. coreJ evaluates one dataset at a time, so the cross-trial claim has no frame here; the fixture pins the implemented reading rather than asserting the rule is wrong. Cross-reference finding SD0083-F1 (INFO). NEUTER CHECK: change row 2's STUDYID to S1 and the count becomes 2."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID  type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
---
S1 | DM | S1-001 | 001
S2 | DM | S1-001 | 001
S1 | DM | S1-002 | 002
